MID_SE_Buc_Sci_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_C_001: Where are you going, Sirocco? Ah, let me guess.\nOff to while away your time with some lady...or five?
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_C_002: How very like you, Buccar, to dismiss what I do as\nthough it didn't serve us all.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_C_003: I've told you before—the women I "while away" my\ntime with provide invaluable information.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_C_004: Please, your philandering is intolerable. Worse yet,\nyou are presumptuous even with Lady Leda!
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_C_005: Ah yes, I should check in on Miss Leda. How I would\nlove to coax her heart out from behind those thorns.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_C_006: A man as callow and fatuous as you has nothing of\nworth to offer her. You are no match.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_C_007: And since we're having this chat, let me make one\nthing clear: you are not to get any closer to milady.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_C_008: Hahaha! You may as well command the wind not to\nblow. I will do as I please.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_C_009: I will never understand why the goddess Kalla\nelevated a man of your caliber to vulkan.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_C_010: Even if she is fond of you, surely there are men\nbetter suited to the job.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_C_011: How dare you suggest that my lady appointed me\npower celestial general out of favoritism.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_C_012: Sirocco...
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_C_013: Be careful what you say, Buccar.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_C_014: I will not tolerate an insult against my lady.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_C_015: Yes...of course. It was...a slip of the tongue.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_C_016: My words were disrespectful to the goddess and to\nher priests. My sincerest apology.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_C_017: Ah, well. As long as you understand, then that's that.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_C_018: I had best be on my way. I have a tryst planned with\na lovely lady and wouldn't want to keep her waiting.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_C_019: For that one moment, it was as if he were a different\nman. Is his loyalty to Kalla truly so deep?
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_C_020: His usual behavior makes it hard to believe.\nBut...perhaps there is a reason for his devotion.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_001: Sirocco, a moment. There is something I still\ndo not understand.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_002: I have regaled my lady Kalla with a thorough report\nand am on my way to town...so no time for lectures.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_003: I heard you. And I do not understand how it is that\nyou show such disrespect to your lady.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_004: Ah, so you were eavesdropping on me. Lovely.\nDo tell—what disrespect do you mean?
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_005: You lean into her as if to toy with her heart, and you\nspeak to her in a way that is so very...irreverent.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_006: And when she scolds you, you simply laugh.\nAre you a child?
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_007: When you snapped at me before, you suddenly had\nthe bearing of a truly loyal man. So I wonder...
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_008: Please. Let's not speak of that moment. I'd be\nembarrassed if my lady heard about it.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_009: What? Why hide it? You defended the goddess you\nserve as a vulkan. It is proof of your deep loyalty.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_010: The word "loyalty" doesn't come close to capturing\nthe feelings I have for my lady.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_011: What do you mean?
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_012: I was abandoned as an infant on the temple of Kalla's\nfront steps.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_013: That day, a rare hailstorm blew in. If I'd remained\nout in the cold any longer, I'd have died.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_014: But...my beloved goddess found me. She scooped me\nup into her arms and brought me inside.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_015: The goddess Kalla herself...took you in?
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_016: In my earliest memories, I am always nestled in her\nlap, surrounded by her priests.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_017: The temple is my home—it's my everything. And\nwhat I give to my lady...
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_018: It is something much more powerful than loyalty\nor faith. There is no other name for it but love.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_019: It seems...I've misunderstood. You repay your lady's\nkindness with every ounce of your soul.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_020: Now that you understand my behavior, I'll be on\nmy way.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_021: No, wait. You've not answered my first question.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_022: I understand the depth of your loyalty, but isn't that\nwhy you ought to pay your lady the utmost respect?
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_023: You still don't get it, do you, Buccar?
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_024: The way I behave is an expression of the boundless\nlove I feel.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_025: And such potent feelings must be sung, spoken...or\nshown with the body itself. They must be expressed.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_026: In other words, the way you've seen me act and\nspeak... It is simply how I show respect to my lady.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_027: Agh. I do not...understand. This is...a way people\nexpress...feelings?
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_028: Now then, I must ask that you never speak of our\nrather...sharp...interaction the other day.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_029: I prefer to be seen as someone light as a breeze. And\nI'd never want my lady to catch sight of the storm.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_B_030: A way to express feelings...hmm...
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_001: What could you possibly need from me at this hour?\nSunset is a time best spent with beautiful women.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_002: We're in the midst of a war. Intruders could descend\nupon us at any time.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_003: As long as we're going to be up keeping watch,\nI figured we may as well have a drink together.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_004: Ah, it's not just any drink you're serving, but a fine\nwine from the south.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_005: Hmm... A shame not to share it with a\nbeautiful woman.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_006: The Demon Bear of Baphos isn't a good enough\ndrinking partner for you?
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_007: You're the one who told me that it is important\nto express feelings.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_008: It does not come easy. I am no great speaker. But\nwith a drink in my hand, I could find my way.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_009: As warriors and as comrades in arms, let's do as you\nsaid. Let's talk and...improve our friendship.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_010: I admit I'm not accustomed to this tactless candor\nof yours, but I wouldn't mind a drink. I'll join you.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_011: *sob* I...am such a fool...
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_012: It would seem even the Demon Bear sheds tears.\nCome now, drink some water. Here.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_013: I've always protected Lady Leda, ever since she was\nbut a wisp of a thing...
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_014: And yet, I could not stop milady from marching\ndown the path towards revenge. I am so disloyal...
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_015: Regardless of the path Miss Leda chose to take, you\nare, without a doubt, loyal.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_016: Even when you played the villain, you were doing\nyour best to protect her.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_017: I have failed... I could never face Lord Guillermo...
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_018: Gods, what an emotional drunk you are!
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_019: Please, Sirocco... I can't do it alone...
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_020: Lady Leda needs your strength... I depend...\non you...too...
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_021: A sleep will do you good. Careless though, seeing\nhow you were so worried about intruders earlier.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_022: Or perhaps this is just a sign of your trust in me?
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_023: Honestly, when it comes to expressing my feelings,\nI prefer to play songs for pretty ladies.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_024: But just this once, I shall play for you...to thank you\nfor the drink.
MID_SE_Buc_Sci_A_025: May it ease your soul and dry your tears. It is a song\nabout deep affection...for a comrade in arms.